Package: lol-on-linux
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: SrDicov <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: games
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/SrDicov/lol-on-linux
Depends: libstdc++6, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcb-shm0, libxext6, libasound2 | libasound2t64, libpulse0, python3, curl, unzip,
 libxml2, libzstd1, zlib1g, libffi8, libbsd0
Recommends: gamemode, xwayland
Description: Unofficial runtime to run Riot's macOS League of Legends client on Linux
 lol-on-linux runs Riot's official macOS League of Legends client on Linux
 through the Darling compatibility layer. It ships a prebuilt Darling runtime
 plus the per-user compatibility overlays; the game itself is downloaded and
 installed by Riot's own installer on first launch.
 .
 WARNING: using this project can get your account permanently banned. This is
 an unofficial project and is not affiliated with Riot Games.
